From 7b2be044e95005f327af06befe677425e22aec22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Etienne Carriere <etienne.carriere@st.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Mar 2026 17:29:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 610/913] core: add notification of non-secure virtual
 interrupt

Send notifications of virtual interrupt events to non-secure world.
These events are intended to be handle by non-secure world from its
interrupt handler. This feature reuses the async notification mechanism
for triggering a asynchronous event in non-secure world.

This feature differs from OP-TE legacy async-notif in that OP-TEE async
notification are all related to OP-TEE thread execution (either
invoking OP-TEE a bottom-half thread or waking up a TEE thread that
is waiting (in non-secure scheduler).

A notified interrupt is an identifier between 0 and NOTIF_IT_VALUE_MAX
managed using a list separated from the async notif ID list. Non-secure
world uses the same async notif mechanism to query pending interrupt
event, using added OPTEE_SMC_GET_IT_NOTIF_VALUE API function ID.

Adds another SMC service to mask/unmask a interrupt notification line.

For the implementation, it_pending bit string contains the pending state
of each IT. It is set when notif_send_it(it number) is called and
cleared during OPTEE_SMC_GET_IT_VALUE.

Bit field it_masked bit string contains the masking state that is set
with OPTEE_SMC_SET_IT_MASK.

This change defines up to 32 interrupt identifiers OP-TEE can notify
to non-secure world. Once core is initialized, all interrupt notifiers
are masked.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 1113f2800eb58222136b386d8b8220dcd8539bda core: add notification of non-secure virtual interrupt]
Co-developed-by: Pascal Paillet <p.paillet@st.com>
Signed-off-by: Pascal Paillet <p.paillet@st.com>
Co-developed-by: Gatien Chevallier <gatien.chevallier@foss.st.com>
Signed-off-by: Gatien Chevallier <gatien.chevallier@foss.st.com>
Co-developed-by: <Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Signed-off-by: Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Signed-off-by: Etienne Carriere <etienne.carriere@st.com>
